{"1-3":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"silas-g4609","name":"Silas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"timothy-g5095g","name":"Timothy","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[{"id":"thessalonica-g2332","name":"Thessalonica","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"words":[{"base":"G3962","lemma":"πατήρ","tr":"patēr","gloss":"father","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":413},{"base":"G0089","lemma":"ἀδιαλείπτως","tr":"adialeiptōs","gloss":"unceasingly","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G2331","lemma":"Θεσσαλονικεύς","tr":"Thessalonikeus","gloss":"Thessalonian","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G4610","lemma":"Σιλουανός","tr":"Silouanos","gloss":"Silvanus","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G5547","lemma":"Χριστός","tr":"Christos","gloss":"Christ","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":529},{"base":"G3417","lemma":"μνεία","tr":"mneia","gloss":"remembrance","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"G2962","lemma":"κύριος","tr":"kurios","gloss":"lord: God","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":714},{"base":"G2424","lemma":"Ἰησοῦς","tr":"Iēsous","gloss":"Jesus","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":911},{"base":"G2873","lemma":"κόπος","tr":"kopos","gloss":"labor","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"G3421","lemma":"μνημονεύω","tr":"mnēmoneuō","gloss":"to remember","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":21}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CO","chapter":13,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":26,"source":"openbible","text":"And now these three remain: faith, hope, and love; but the greatest of these is love.","from":3},{"book":"REV","chapter":2,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"I know your deeds—your love, your faith, your service, your perseverance—and your latest deeds are greater than your first.","from":3},{"book":"ROM","chapter":1,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"First, I thank my God through Jesus Christ for all of you, because your faith is being proclaimed all over the world.","from":2},{"book":"ROM","chapter":1,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"God, whom I serve with my spirit in preaching the gospel of His Son, is my witness how constantly I remember you","from":2},{"book":"GAL","chapter":5,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision nor uncircumcision has any value. What matters is faith, expressing itself through love.","from":3},{"book":"ROM","chapter":1,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"To all in Rome who are loved by God and called to be saints: Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.","from":1},{"book":"EPH","chapter":1,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"For this reason, ever since I heard about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all the saints,","from":2},{"book":"EPH","chapter":1,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"I have not stopped giving thanks for you, remembering you in my prayers,","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":4},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"4-10":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":10}],"places":[{"id":"achaia-g0882","name":"Achaia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"macedonia-g3109","name":"Macedonia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":7}],"words":[{"base":"G1096","lemma":"γίνομαι","tr":"ginomai","gloss":"to be","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":668},{"base":"G0882","lemma":"Ἀχαΐα","tr":"Achaia","gloss":"Achaia","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"G3109","lemma":"Μακεδονία","tr":"Makedonia","gloss":"Macedonia","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":22},{"base":"G3056","lemma":"λόγος","tr":"logos","gloss":"word","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":329},{"base":"G4314","lemma":"πρός","tr":"pros","gloss":"to","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":700},{"base":"G5620","lemma":"ὥστε","tr":"hōste","gloss":"so","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":83},{"base":"G3441","lemma":"μόνος","tr":"monos","gloss":"alone","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":111},{"base":"G1537","lemma":"ἐκ","tr":"ek","gloss":"out from","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":913},{"base":"G0040","lemma":"ἅγιος","tr":"hagios","gloss":"holy","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":222},{"base":"G6063","lemma":"οἶδα","tr":"oida","gloss":"to know","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":283}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1TH","chapter":5,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":23,"source":"openbible","text":"For God has not appointed us to suffer wrath, but to obtain salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ.","from":10},{"book":"2TH","chapter":2,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"But we should always thank God for you, brothers who are loved by the Lord, because God has chosen you from the beginning to be saved by the sanctification of the Spirit and by faith in the truth.","from":4},{"book":"TIT","chapter":2,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"In everything, show yourself to be an example by doing good works. In your teaching show integrity, dignity,","from":7},{"book":"1CO","chapter":11,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"You are to imitate me, just as I imitate Christ.","from":6},{"book":"ISA","chapter":25,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"He will swallow up death forever. The Lord GOD will wipe away the tears from every face and remove the disgrace of His people from the whole earth. For the LORD has spoken.","from":10},{"book":"ISA","chapter":25,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"And in that day it will be said, “Surely this is our God; we have waited for Him, and He has saved us. This is the LORD for whom we have waited. Let us rejoice and be glad in His salvation.”","from":10},{"book":"ACT","chapter":13,"verse":52,"verseEnd":52,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"And the disciples were filled with joy and with the Holy Spirit.","from":6},{"book":"1CO","chapter":4,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"Therefore I urge you to imitate me.","from":6}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}